# Website gap spacing

When adding or changing `gap` on the storefront, always use **gap-3**.

| Context | Value |
|---------|--------|
| Tailwind | `gap-3` |
| CSS | `gap: 0.75rem` or `gap: var(--gap)` |

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
<div className="flex gap-3">
<div className="grid grid-cols-4 gap-3">

// ❌ BAD
<div className="flex gap-2">
<div className="grid gap-6">
<div className="grid gap-8">
```

```css
/* ✅ GOOD */
.combo-grid { gap: var(--gap); }

/* ❌ BAD */
.combo-grid { gap: 1.5rem; }
```

## Exceptions

- `gap: 0` only when items must sit flush (no spacing).
- Do not invent other gap scales (`gap-1`, `gap-4`, `1rem`, `2rem`, etc.) for website layout.
